<header><p class="st-kicker">electorate · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Electorate of Cologne</h1><p class="st-meta">953 CE – 1803 CE (approx.) · capital Bonn</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The prince-archbishopric of Cologne, one of the seven electors, whose archbishops crowned German kings and ruled a long strip of the Rhineland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-cologne">Cologne</a> had been an archbishopric since the 8th century. In 953 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i-duke-of-bavaria">Otto I</a> made his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruno-the-great">Bruno</a> archbishop and also duke of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-lotharingia">Lotharingia</a>, founding the temporal power of the see. Grants of counties and, in 1180, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-westphalia">Duchy of Westphalia</a> after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> made the archbishops major territorial princes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a> confirmed the archbishop as one of the seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> and arch-chancellor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. After long conflicts with the citizens and the archbishop's defeat at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-worringen">Battle of Worringen</a> in 1288, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-cologne">Cologne</a> became in effect a free city, and the electors moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonn">Bonn</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wittelsbach">Wittelsbach</a> family held the see from 1583 to 1761, building the palaces at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruhl-rhineland">Brühl</a> and Bonn.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-occupation-of-the-netherlands">French revolutionary armies</a> took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> in 1794, and the electorate was dissolved in 1803; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> went to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse">Hesse-Darmstadt</a> and other lands to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-nassau">Nassau</a>. After 1815 the territories became Prussian. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-cologne">Cologne</a> Cathedral, begun in 1248, was completed in 1880.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/electorate-of-cologne.jpg" alt="Electorate of Cologne" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Laurens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_St_George%27s_Cross.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>953 CE – 1803 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>electorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bonn</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bruno the Great, Rainald of Dassel, Clemens August of Bavaria</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ripuarian German, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Archbishopric of Cologne, Kurköln</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1378&amp;focus=electorate-of-cologne" aria-label="Electorate of Cologne on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4842 417 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Electorate of Cologne lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5162 673L5199 691M5162 673L5229 694M5162 673L5054 728M5162 673L5183 654M5162 673L5158 667"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5199 691h0M5229 694h0M5054 728h0M5183 654h0M5158 667h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5162 673h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5162 673h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bonn. <a href="/atlas?year